/vendor/
# /composer.lock is deliberately NOT ignored: the tracked lock is the corpus
# the S440 security-audit gate audits (scripts/security-audit-check.php reads
# the committed lock; its CI job asserts the whole-file audit posture). Do not
# `git rm --cached` it.
/.phpunit.cache/
/coverage-report/
/coverage.xml
/build/
.caliber/
# Ignore all Claude CLI personal files and state.
# NB `.claude/*` not `.claude/` — git never descends into an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY,
# so with `.claude/` the four `!` negations below are silently INERT and none of
# these files can be staged (tracking was 0 despite the negations). Excluding the
# directory's CONTENTS instead lets the negations take effect. Verified:
# `git check-ignore -v .claude/rules/schema-changes.md` used to report the `.claude/`
# line as the match (rc=0); with `.claude/*` it now reports no match (rc=1). This
# brings phlix-shared in line with phlix-server/phlix-hub, which already track this tree.
.claude/*
# S-shared-04 tracks settings.json per its acceptance ("expect settings.json"),
# UNLIKE phlix-server/phlix-hub which deliberately leave `.claude/settings.json`
# ignored. CAVEAT: this file hardcodes an absolute, machine- and node-version-
# specific interpreter path (`/home/<user>/.nvm/versions/node/vX/bin/caliber`,
# 4x), so on any clone lacking that path the caliber hooks will not resolve until
# the commands are made portable (e.g. `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` / PATH lookup).
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/hooks/
.opencode/node_modules/
.opencode/memory/
.opencode/.env
